---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Meeting Easy - Support"
  description="Get help with Meeting Easy - Meeting Notes for iPhone, iPad and Mac."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/meeting-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Meeting Easy?</p>
          <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Meeting%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <div class="space-y-8 text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I record a meeting?</h3>
            <p>Tap Record. On a Mac, you can also start from Meeting Easy in the menu bar. The meeting opens with a live transcript. Tap Stop when it's over, and Meeting Easy writes the summary, the decisions and the action items.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I record both sides of a call on a Mac?</h3>
            <p>Start recording before or during the call. The first time, allow Meeting Easy to record the audio the Mac plays. Your microphone is transcribed as Me and everyone else as Others. Record the other people on calls in Settings turns this on and off.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Why doesn't my meeting have notes?</h3>
            <p>Summaries, action items and answers use Apple Intelligence, which needs a device that supports it with Apple Intelligence turned on in Settings, and a language Apple Intelligence supports. Without it, Meeting Easy still records and transcribes your meetings.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I record with the screen locked?</h3>
            <p>Yes. On iPhone and iPad, Meeting Easy keeps recording with the screen locked or while you use another app. A phone call pauses the recording until it ends.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do my meetings get to my other devices?</h3>
            <p>Sign in to the same iCloud account on each device, with iCloud turned on for Meeting Easy. Meetings sync on their own, including one that's still being recorded. Settings shows when they last synced, or what's in the way.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How does Up next work?</h3>
            <p>Allow calendar access, and today's meetings show under Up next. Tap the record button beside one to record it with the event's name and the people invited. You can also link a meeting to an event after recording.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What can I ask about a meeting?</h3>
            <p>Open a meeting, choose Ask, and ask anything, such as "What did we decide about pricing?" or "What are my action items?" Answers come from what was said, with times you can tap to hear that moment.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Which languages does Meeting Easy support?</h3>
            <p>Meeting Easy transcribes in your device's language when Apple's on-device speech recognition supports it. Summaries and answers are available in the languages Apple Intelligence supports.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Where is my data stored?</h3>
            <p>On your devices and in your own iCloud, and nowhere else. To save space, turn off Keep the audio in Settings, and Meeting Easy keeps only the transcript and notes. Deleting a meeting deletes it from all your devices.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
